 \thispagestyle{fancy}
+\phantomsection
 \addcontentsline{toc}{chapter}{General Conclusion and Perspectives}
 \section*{Summary of the Work}
 This work set out to measure, rather than assume, how a local, open-source Whisper-based pipeline performs on noisy multilingual speech and how far low-cost mitigations close the resulting gap. The engineering objectives were achieved: a licensed trilingual evaluation set was assembled (SO1), a configurable \textit{faster-whisper} pipeline was implemented (SO2), and a pre-specified 180-run CPU campaign plus 288 extension runs were completed without recorded runtime errors (SO3). The broader scientific objective is only partially met because the available corpus represents single-speaker banking telephony rather than corporate meetings. The contribution is therefore a reproducible pilot and component analysis, not a deployment validation.

